From afc4c1a7a78b10c9c969f5cc012f301bd1f03651 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "David C. Manuelda" <StormByte@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:24:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(logger): group human-readable numbers without a libc
 locale

en_US.UTF-8 is the default number locale. musl does not provide its
grouping, and the C fallback printed 1000. When a named locale has an
empty numpunct grouping, format with en_US separators so 1000 stays
1,000. A real locale that already groups is left unchanged, and C and
POSIX stay ungrouped.

Record the correction under Unreleased.
---
